# Smoke test after plans (ALGR)

When you finish implementing a **plan**, a multi-step feature, or other **shippable** work, run a **smoke test at the appropriate timing** before ending the turn as done.

## When

- After executing an agreed plan (or a substantial slice of one).
- After shippable UI/API/Worker changes that should work on the running host.
- Before marking related Linear issues Done (pair with completion notes).

## What “appropriate” means

- Hit the changed path in the running app (local URL, health endpoint, or `version.json` as relevant).
- Prefer an automated check when the product already has one; otherwise a short manual/browser or curl smoke of the happy path.
- If deploy is required (`ship-after-change`), smoke **after** publish when that is how truth is verified.

## Do not

- Claim “done” on plan implementation with zero verification.
- Skip smoke because unit tests passed if the change is integration/runtime-facing.
- Block forever on unavailable environments — note what could not be smoked and why.
